{"sheets":[{"name":"Wall_Comparison","rows":[["RIVERKNOLL RENEWAL | WALLS ALONE: SYSTEM 3E vs 2x6 TIMBER vs PREFAB PANELS (v1, Nov 26 2026)","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""],["Asked by the organizer: what the walls alone cost to buy, ship and put up for each system, what each saves a year, when the extra cost pays back, and the 50-year total in today's money. Same building in every column: 744 beds, a concrete slab on grade with vinyl plank inside, timber upper floors, timber roof trusses (model v24.3). Blue cells are inputs; every other number is a formula. Sources at the bottom (S1-S12). \"Estimate\" means no source was found and the number is ours.","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""],["Plain answer, base case: for the outside walls alone, System 3E imported from Poland today costs $35.22 per sq ft of wall, against $24.25 for 2x6 timber with R-5 foam and $25.24 for prefab panels. That is about $4,560 a bed more than timber all in, and its $42 a bed-year of savings never pays that back. System 3E beats timber on day one ($20.50) only if a US plant sells blocks near $12 per sq ft of wall delivered. The whole System 3E building with timber upper floors costs $2,318 a bed more than timber at that US price (paid back in year 23 only if the insurance saving holds) and $17,069 a bed more with blocks imported today (never paid back).","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""],["1. QUANTITIES (model v24.3)","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""],["Beds","744","beds","S1","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""],["Gross floor area","301,920","GSF","S1","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""],["Net exterior wall per GSF (after windows and doors)","0.52","SF wall/GSF","S1","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""],["Exterior w